# Feature 1: SQLite Infrastructure - COMPLETED

## Summary
Implemented SQLite infrastructure with connection manager and migrations for all required tables.

## Files Modified/Created
- `internal/adapters/sync/sqlite/sqlite.go` - Added Ping() method to connection manager
- `internal/adapters/sync/sqlite/migrations.go` - Updated sessions and drift_log table schemas
- `internal/adapters/sync/sqlite/sqlite_test.go` - Created comprehensive tests for connection manager
- `internal/adapters/sync/sqlite/migrations_test.go` - Created comprehensive tests for migrations

## Changes Made

### Connection Manager (sqlite.go)
- Added `Ping()` method to test database connectivity
- Existing methods: `Open()`, `Close()`, `DB()`, `Path()`, `IsClosed()`

### Migrations (migrations.go)
Updated schemas to match requirements:

#### sessions table
Updated to include all required fields:
- id, workspace_id, backend, model, profile, status
- tokens_used, tokens_limit, pid, machine_id
- started_at, last_active_at

#### drift_log table
Updated to include all required fields:
- id, workspace_id, session_id
- original_focus, detected_topic, prompt_snippet, action_taken
- created_at

#### Other tables (unchanged as they matched requirements)
- workspaces: id, name, repo_path, worktree_path, branch, focus, status, default_backend, last_active_at, created_at
- checkpoints: id, workspace_id, session_id, summary, details, files_modified, decisions, machine_id, created_at
- context_items: id, name, type, content, tags, token_estimate, last_used_at, created_at
- rules: id, name, content, scope, is_active, created_at

### Indices Added
- idx_sessions_last_active
- idx_sessions_backend

## Test Coverage
All 18 tests pass:
- Connection lifecycle (Open, Close, Ping, DB)
- In-memory database support
- Concurrent access safety
- All table creation and CRUD operations
- Foreign key constraints
- Cascade delete behavior
- Index creation verification
- Default value verification
- Migration idempotency

## Dependencies
- github.com/mattn/go-sqlite3 v1.14.22 (already in go.mod)
